            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: Are site excavation projects in Carlisle, MA subject to Conservation Commission approval?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates reviews all property boundary maps and wetland proximity indicators with the Carlisle Conservation Commission prior to initiating land clearing or earthmoving. Any excavation, grading, or paving performed within the 100-foot wetland buffer zone or 200-foot riverfront resource area requires an Order of Conditions. S. Phaneuf & Associates installs double-row staked straw wattles and silt fencing to maintain full environmental compliance throughout Carlisle projects.</p>

            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: How long does a professionally installed asphalt driveway last in Carlisle, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates builds asphalt driveways in Carlisle engineered to last 20 to 30 years. Driveway longevity depends on proper sub-base gravel depth (6 to 8 inches minimum), full compaction with 3-to-5 ton vibratory rollers, and applying MassDOT-certified hot mix asphalt. Regular sealcoating every 3 to 4 years protects the asphalt surface against snowplow scrape marks, oil penetration, and severe winter frost heave.</p>
